# Curated per-target test262 excludes for windows/arm64, passed to run-test262
# via -x (see all_test.go). Use this file for tests that fail ONLY in the Go
# build (Go/libc numeric discrepancies) and therefore are NOT captured by the
# native C reference run in generator.go's genTargetConf. Native/upstream and
# universal excludes belong in the auto-generated test262_<os>_<arch>.conf and
# in the base test262.conf respectively.
#
# NOTE: unlike windows/amd64, cosh-approx is NOT excluded here -- on arm64 the
# Go compiler FMA-contracts, which happens to make modernc.org/libc's Cosh match
# the reference constant; only Sinh still drifts. Same arm64 behaviour as
# darwin/arm64 and freebsd/arm64.

# https://gitlab.com/cznic/libquickjs/-/issues/5
# sinh-approx: the same Go/libc Sinh discrepancy already excluded on darwin/arm64
# and freebsd/arm64. Native C QuickJS PASSES this (system libm sinh); it fails
# only in the Go build because modernc.org/libc's Sinh drifts a couple ULP from
# the reference constant: got 1.1667648891489082e-7, expected near
# 1.166764889148908e-7 (relative error 2).
test262/test/staging/sm/Math/sinh-approx.js
